 "notes": "No repeating bay module; one-off modern facade. Reveal grooves are listed one by one about every 1.75 m, read from the grey panel wall. They are drawn full width, but in reality they appear only on the grey panel wall and the angled entry wall, not across the left glazed block. The entry recess and the curved glass-block drum are flattened onto the wall plane. The door position is approximate because of the overhang shadow and the sun glare. | Whole Beach St front was under scaffolding with plastic-wrapped decks in 2022 and largely hidden by street trees. The EVEREST Waterproofing banner is a temporary contractor sign on the scaffold and is omitted. Module is a concrete pier with two windows per floor, then a dark recessed louvre slot: about 8 bays at a period of 79.69/8 = 9.96 m. The module was re-phased so a window pair centres under the banner (about u=43 m); the rhythm is carried through the hidden stretches. Window sizes and floor heights are estimated. No shopfronts or tenants on this wall. Low hedge along the base is not mode | Plain light-grey concrete office side wall with no shops. There are two blue ribbon windows: one on the second floor across the right half, and one on the set-back top floor. A narrow window sits above the recessed slot door at about 10 m. The ground floor has a roll-up louvred grille, dark slot doors and a boarded door. The left 0-12 m is heavily obscured by trees and shade; upper windows there could not be read and were left out.",
